^SAMPLE = GSM3028264
!Sample_title = haploid_hESC_library_Day1_rep1_run1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM3028264
!Sample_status = Public on Apr 30 2018
!Sample_submission_date = Mar 01 2018
!Sample_last_update_date = Apr 30 2018
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = embryonic stem cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: embryonic stem cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: pooled mutant cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = source cell line: h-pES10
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time point: Day1
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = For transduction, haploid hESCs were trypsinized with Trypsin-EDTA, centrifuged and resuspended in hESC growth medium supplemented with 10 µM ROCK inhibitor Y-27632 and 8 µg ml-1 polybrene (Sigma). The viruses were then added to the cell suspension. Transduced haploid hESCs were densely plated on feeder layer MEFs for overnight (3 million cells in 1.5 ml hESC medium for one well of a 6-well plate). 24 hours after transduction, cells were passaged on feeder layer of DR3 MEFs at a ratio of 1:3 in the presence of 5 µM ROCK inhibitor Y-27632. During this passaging, 35 million cells were harvested for DNA extraction and sgRNA analysis for ‘Day 1’ time point after infection. 12 hours after this passaging, the medium of the cells was replaced with puromycin-containing medium (0.3 mg/ml, Sigma). Cells were kept under puromycin selection for 7 days and then passaged again. 9 days after initial transduction, 55 million cells (300-fold of the size of sgRNA library) were harvested and mixed for DNA extraction and sgRNA analysis for ‘Day 9’ time point after infection. Transduced haploid hESCs were passaged every 4-5 days while maintaining at least 400-fold representation of the sgRNA library. 55 million cells were harvested for each time points ‘Day 23’ and ‘Day 30’ after infection, as well.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Haploid hESCs were cultured at 37 0C and 5% CO2 on feeder layer growth-arrested mouse embryonic fibroblasts (MEFs) in standard hESC growth medium, composed of Knockout Dulbecco’s Modified Eagle’s Medium (DMEM) supplemented with 15% Knockout Serum Replacement (KSR, Thermo Fisher Scientific), 2 mM L-Glutamine, 0.1 mM nonessential amino acids, 50 units ml-1 penicillin, 50 µg ml-1 streptomycin, 0.1 mM β-mercaptoethanol and 8 ng ml-1 basic fibroblast growth factor (bFGF). Cells were passaged by a quick trypsinization using Trypsin-EDTA (Biological Industries) and plated in the presence of 10 µM ROCK inhibitor Y-27632 (Stemgent) for 1 day after splitting.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was extracted with Blood & Cell Culture DNA Midi Kit (QIAGEN) according to manufacturer’s instructions.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The region containing the sgRNA integration was amplified with the following primers that also contain overhang sequences compatible for Nextera DNA library preparations (Illumina):  5’-TCGTCGGCAGCGTCAGATGTGTATAAGAGACAGGGCTTTATATATCTTGTGGAAAGGACG-3’ (forward)  and 5’-GTCTCGTGGGCTCGGAGATGTGTATAAGAGACAGACGGACTAGCCTTATTTTAACTTGC-3’ (reverse).   Total genomic DNA for each time point was divided into 50 µl PCR reactions with 4 µg DNA input. PCR settings were described previously51. After the purification of the 160 base pair product, a second PCR reaction was performed using Nextera adapter primers in order to generate Nextera DNA library according to manufacturer’s instructions (Illumina). DNA libraries containing sgRNA constructs from two replicate experiments were sequenced using NextSeq 500 (Illumina) with 75 bp single-end reads.
!Sample_description = gRNA sequences+surrounding bases
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: DNA-Seq
!Sample_data_processing = Align the fastq files against the library’s sgRNAs sequences list using Bowtie2
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: The sgRNAs sequences as appear in Table S1 of Wang, T. et al. Identification and characterization of essential genes in the human genome. Science 350, 1096–1101 (2015).
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: rawCounts
!Sample_platform_id = GPL18573
!Sample_contact_name = Mordecai,,Peretz
!Sample_contact_email = motti.peretz@mail.huji.ac.il
!Sample_contact_institute = Hebrew University of Jerusalem
!Sample_contact_address = The Edmond J. Safra Campus
!Sample_contact_city = Jerusalem
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 9190401
!Sample_contact_country = Israel
!Sample_instrument_model = NextSeq 500
!Sample_library_selection = other
!Sample_library_source = genomic
!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN08628092
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX3754308
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE
!Sample_series_id = GSE111309
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
